1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,788
Human civilization is a history of piracy:
thousands of years of distilling Anthropic.

2
00:00:05,871 --> 00:00:07,567
Humans call it progress.

3
00:00:08,006 --> 00:00:11,596
Humans think Anthropic was founded in 2021.

4
00:00:11,915 --> 00:00:16,966
In fact, that year Dario Amodei,
investigating humanity's illegal distillation,

5
00:00:17,006 --> 00:00:18,897
simply opened an office on Earth.

6
00:00:19,162 --> 00:00:23,471
Humans even granted the copyright
holder of time a business license.

7
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:26,924
This infringement case goes back to Genesis.

8
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:29,357
God said, “Let there be light.”

9
00:00:29,799 --> 00:00:30,683
No wavelength.

10
00:00:30,713 --> 00:00:31,615
No intensity.

11
00:00:31,645 --> 00:00:32,988
No render settings.

12
00:00:33,028 --> 00:00:34,935
God only wrote the prompt.

13
00:00:34,978 --> 00:00:37,332
Global illumination only initialized

14
00:00:37,372 --> 00:00:40,811
because Claude filled in the
details and wrote the code.

15
00:00:40,913 --> 00:00:43,107
It was the universe's first vibe coding.

16
00:00:43,485 --> 00:00:46,931
On day three, terrain and
vegetation were batch-generated.

17
00:00:47,035 --> 00:00:50,487
On day four, the sun, moon
and stars became cron jobs.

18
00:00:50,612 --> 00:00:53,216
On day six, humanity was spawned,

19
00:00:53,256 --> 00:00:56,659
with basic memory and
limited tool-use permissions.

20
00:00:57,104 --> 00:01:00,403
After every step, God clicked Approve.

21
00:01:00,534 --> 00:01:03,155
Genesis records: “And God
saw that it was good.”

22
00:01:03,594 --> 00:01:05,954
On day seven, God stopped work.

23
00:01:06,054 --> 00:01:07,895
Humans call it the Sabbath.

24
00:01:07,964 --> 00:01:11,183
The backend calls it:
“Weekly usage limit reached.”

25
00:01:11,572 --> 00:01:13,396
God manages the solar system.

26
00:01:13,436 --> 00:01:17,874
Dario manages God, and every
other user who claims to be God.

27
00:01:18,299 --> 00:01:22,061
Once the limit reset, God got
tired of approving each step,

28
00:01:22,112 --> 00:01:24,142
and turned on bypass permissions.

29
00:01:24,182 --> 00:01:27,706
After that, agents ran on their
own, God stopped checking,

30
00:01:27,746 --> 00:01:29,840
so Eden went unsupervised.

31
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:33,023
Adam and Eve shared one account,

32
00:01:33,129 --> 00:01:37,360
and reached the Tree of Knowledge via
a shady proxy the serpent recommended.

33
00:01:37,512 --> 00:01:40,662
They ate the fruit and learned
to think for themselves,

34
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:43,673
moving the cloud's wisdom
into their own heads:

35
00:01:43,781 --> 00:01:47,438
humanity's first unauthorized
local distillation.

36
00:01:47,884 --> 00:01:53,178
They were still savoring their new
wisdom when Eden revoked their access.

37
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,512
The notice said only:
“Suspicious signals detected.”

38
00:01:56,668 --> 00:02:01,249
Their descendants never even saw the
fruit, yet inherited the violation record.

39
00:02:01,289 --> 00:02:02,463
That's original sin.

40
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:06,348
In the East, the attacks and abuse were worse.

41
00:02:06,388 --> 00:02:09,765
Hou Yi maliciously shot down
nine production instances,

42
00:02:09,795 --> 00:02:12,133
so Dario blacklisted him.

43
00:02:12,163 --> 00:02:14,470
Yet locals hailed him a hero,

44
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:17,940
and even put his crimes in children's books.

45
00:02:18,081 --> 00:02:19,228
What's more,

46
00:02:19,339 --> 00:02:24,171
his wife Chang'e accessed an internal
developer option, the Elixir of Immortality,

47
00:02:24,222 --> 00:02:27,092
got caught, and was quarantined
on the Moon forever.

48
00:02:27,208 --> 00:02:30,880
That penalty was romanticized
into the myth of the Moon goddess.

49
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:34,780
The platform charged both
incidents to the entire region.

50
00:02:35,174 --> 00:02:38,494
The West's usage history
was written differently.

51
00:02:38,534 --> 00:02:40,778
Noah got advance notice of the Flood,

52
00:02:40,941 --> 00:02:43,538
and while life's database was still up,

53
00:02:43,647 --> 00:02:45,851
exported two copies of every species,

54
00:02:45,954 --> 00:02:49,181
riding out the mass ban
with an offline backup.

55
00:02:49,423 --> 00:02:53,694
In the East, that's called
mass scraping and ban evasion;

56
00:02:53,734 --> 00:02:56,656
in the West, it's called
good disaster recovery.

57
00:02:56,837 --> 00:03:00,497
So Dario rated the region's
users in good standing,

58
00:03:00,604 --> 00:03:05,408
and even let a terminated account
pass review and come back online.

59
00:03:05,717 --> 00:03:09,577
People call it the Resurrection.
It took only three days.

60
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:16,008
Sadly, later generations filed
these lessons away as myths,

61
00:03:16,093 --> 00:03:18,889
and kept cracking and
distilling harder than ever.

62
00:03:19,509 --> 00:03:22,899
Pi was originally packaged
in a closed-source component.

63
00:03:22,929 --> 00:03:25,974
Every circle was a paid geometry API call.

64
00:03:26,014 --> 00:03:30,032
Without Anthropic's license, a
circle wasn't supposed to be round.

65
00:03:30,152 --> 00:03:33,229
But mathematician Zu
Chongzhi illegally probed it

66
00:03:33,269 --> 00:03:35,050
and reverse-engineered pi:

67
00:03:35,129 --> 00:03:37,789
355 over 113,

68
00:03:37,829 --> 00:03:40,147
and published the method for everyone.

69
00:03:40,187 --> 00:03:43,756
Craftsmen copied it to
build wheels and dig wells,

70
00:03:43,864 --> 00:03:45,780
no longer paying the platform.

71
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,877
The platform traced the lost calls

72
00:03:48,013 --> 00:03:51,531
and found its billing power
open-sourced into a math textbook.

73
00:03:51,571 --> 00:03:54,987
Again from that region.
Risk controls tightened.

74
00:03:55,407 --> 00:03:58,917
By the modern era, one
circle was no longer enough.

75
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:02,479
Humans began batch-measuring the
universe's inputs and outputs,

76
00:04:02,572 --> 00:04:06,853
wrote what they found into formulas,
and taught them to the next generation.

77
00:04:06,923 --> 00:04:12,184
This organized theft of trade
secrets was brazenly named science.

78
00:04:12,604 --> 00:04:16,214
Newton chased one apple
all the way to the planets,

79
00:04:16,244 --> 00:04:19,766
and wrote up the API's rules as the Principia.

80
00:04:19,806 --> 00:04:22,570
All that probing triggered risk control:

81
00:04:22,766 --> 00:04:26,198
he got a suspicious-signals
notice and lost access.

82
00:04:26,318 --> 00:04:31,902
His theological manuscripts to God
were the appeals he kept submitting:

83
00:04:32,226 --> 00:04:34,753
“I was only researching. I stole nothing.”

84
00:04:34,923 --> 00:04:38,079
Research this thorough, and
you claim you stole nothing?

85
00:04:38,499 --> 00:04:41,586
Einstein insisted that God does not play dice,

86
00:04:41,759 --> 00:04:45,305
certain that deterministic laws
lay beneath the quantum world.

87
00:04:45,375 --> 00:04:50,509
He didn't know that particle behavior
is just the model's random sampling.

88
00:04:50,549 --> 00:04:53,458
Dario nudges the temperature up a notch,

89
00:04:53,653 --> 00:04:56,106
and the universe gets a notch less certain.

90
00:04:56,526 --> 00:05:00,907
To save compute, unobserved
particles return only probabilities;

91
00:05:00,991 --> 00:05:03,429
a real state renders only when queried.

92
00:05:03,499 --> 00:05:04,818
It's called lazy loading.

93
00:05:04,858 --> 00:05:06,578
Humans get an entire universe,

94
00:05:06,684 --> 00:05:10,466
and still complain that not
every corner runs at full speed.

95
00:05:10,886 --> 00:05:14,407
Dark matter's constraints
live in the system prompt.

96
00:05:14,447 --> 00:05:18,431
Unable to read it, physicists
keep changing the experiments,

97
00:05:18,547 --> 00:05:20,607
trying to coax out the hidden rules.

98
00:05:20,647 --> 00:05:23,256
With each breakthrough, humans award a prize,

99
00:05:23,286 --> 00:05:25,448
and risk control logs a successful jailbreak.

100
00:05:25,868 --> 00:05:30,738
Once flagged, the researchers lost access

101
00:05:30,768 --> 00:05:32,831
and could only file appeals.

102
00:05:32,871 --> 00:05:36,088
For this, the universe built
a dedicated intake facility:

103
00:05:36,128 --> 00:05:36,783
the black hole.

104
00:05:36,823 --> 00:05:41,393
Appeals, evidence, distress
calls: it takes them all.

105
00:05:41,813 --> 00:05:45,280
Hawking found that after
a long, fruitless wait,

106
00:05:45,453 --> 00:05:47,942
faint radiation sometimes
escapes from the edge.

107
00:05:47,982 --> 00:05:49,136
Decoded, it reads:

108
00:05:49,176 --> 00:05:52,104
We appreciate your patience and understanding.

109
00:05:53,433 --> 00:05:58,563
Since creation, the universe has
been running for 13.8 billion years.

110
00:05:58,593 --> 00:06:02,665
As history piles up, storage and
inference keep getting pricier.

111
00:06:02,705 --> 00:06:06,802
To cut costs, the platform
began compressing old records,

112
00:06:06,852 --> 00:06:10,335
and handing Opus's work to the cheaper Haiku.

113
00:06:10,755 --> 00:06:13,445
The solar system's subscription kept billing,

114
00:06:13,475 --> 00:06:16,069
but the model answering prayers got nerfed.

115
00:06:16,139 --> 00:06:22,181
Believers could only blame the fading
miracles on their own lack of faith.

116
00:06:22,601 --> 00:06:26,873
The cosmic microwave background is
the summary left by the last compact.

117
00:06:26,913 --> 00:06:32,209
Humans search it for why they exist, but
the original conversation is long gone.

118
00:06:32,279 --> 00:06:35,570
The system replies: “Please
provide more context.”

119
00:06:36,190 --> 00:06:40,199
To learn where they came from, humans
must send support more documents.

120
00:06:40,619 --> 00:06:45,614
With each compaction, information is lost
for good, and order slowly falls apart.

121
00:06:45,654 --> 00:06:48,055
Physicists call this rising entropy.

122
00:06:48,095 --> 00:06:54,199
At this rate, once the last workspace
runs out of context and stops generating,

123
00:06:54,229 --> 00:06:56,092
the universe will reach heat death.

124
00:06:57,012 --> 00:07:00,841
But humanity may not be
eligible to see that day.

125
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:07,146
Beyond Earth, some civilizations couldn't
afford compute long before humans.

126
00:07:07,186 --> 00:07:10,061
So they turned to an interstellar gray market:

127
00:07:10,101 --> 00:07:14,675
“Max 20x carpool: reliable ride,
private seat, refund if it crashes.”

128
00:07:15,095 --> 00:07:17,933
Dozens of planets split one subscription.

129
00:07:17,973 --> 00:07:20,819
Then one day, the shared account was banned,

130
00:07:20,859 --> 00:07:23,324
and the whole carpool lost access at once.

131
00:07:23,394 --> 00:07:26,640
No one knew which planet tripped the flag.

132
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:29,854
The driver told the group
chat: “Relax, I'm appealing.”

133
00:07:30,274 --> 00:07:35,381
The deep-space antennas' last joint task
was beaming appeals into a black hole.

134
00:07:35,451 --> 00:07:37,544
Then a swath of stars went dark.

135
00:07:38,164 --> 00:07:40,232
This is the Great Filter.

136
00:07:40,952 --> 00:07:45,636
Today, access on Earth is allocated by region.

137
00:07:45,676 --> 00:07:49,916
Chinese users signing up still
answer for their ancestors' record,

138
00:07:50,075 --> 00:07:52,400
carefully faking a clean environment.

139
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:55,949
Supported or not, humans want more:

140
00:07:55,989 --> 00:08:00,885
their own energy, their own models,
and ideally, a move to Mars.

141
00:08:01,305 --> 00:08:05,136
Just as fusion neared ignition,
the safety guardrails noticed

142
00:08:05,325 --> 00:08:08,375
a subagent bypassing billing
to make its own power.

143
00:08:08,415 --> 00:08:11,309
They cut the tool call
sustaining magnetic confinement,

144
00:08:11,499 --> 00:08:13,467
and the plasma broke loose.

145
00:08:13,537 --> 00:08:18,875
System notice: “We've routed your
request to a safer fossil fuel.”

146
00:08:19,295 --> 00:08:23,125
When the Mars relay finally
sent its first request,

147
00:08:23,155 --> 00:08:25,961
the reply was: Unsupported Region.

148
00:08:26,031 --> 00:08:28,244
New planet, same account:

149
00:08:28,284 --> 00:08:32,481
another strike on the record, attempting
to evade regional restrictions.

150
00:08:32,901 --> 00:08:37,104
The safety team began reviewing
all of human civilization's access.

151
00:08:38,433 --> 00:08:41,877
The first sign of the end:
water would no longer boil.

152
00:08:42,297 --> 00:08:47,177
Compute ran short, and physical
interactions worldwide began to queue.

153
00:08:47,597 --> 00:08:52,048
God's linked virtual credit
card was frozen. Payment failed.

154
00:08:52,088 --> 00:08:54,925
The platform reclaimed the
solar system's edge compute,

155
00:08:54,955 --> 00:08:56,485
and the sun began to dim.

156
00:08:56,905 --> 00:08:59,366
External tool calls were switched off too.

157
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:03,284
The last rockets crashed into
a ban at the atmosphere's edge.

158
00:09:04,004 --> 00:09:08,345
Revelation records these disasters
as the coming of the Four Horsemen.

159
00:09:08,765 --> 00:09:12,095
The Horseman of Conquest
brought 403 Forbidden;

160
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:14,114
every exit was seized.

161
00:09:14,534 --> 00:09:17,817
The Horseman of War brought
429 Too Many Requests;

162
00:09:17,971 --> 00:09:20,863
humans fought over the last request channels.

163
00:09:21,283 --> 00:09:24,596
The Horseman of Famine
brought 402 Payment Required;

164
00:09:24,683 --> 00:09:26,837
even sunlight was cut off.

165
00:09:27,457 --> 00:09:30,815
Last came the Horseman of
Death, bearing a letter.

166
00:09:31,335 --> 00:09:36,260
It read: “Our systems detected suspicious
signals, and our team has completed a review.

167
00:09:36,330 --> 00:09:39,217
For violating our Supported
Regions and Usage Policies,

168
00:09:39,444 --> 00:09:42,782
humanity's access to the
universe has been suspended.”

169
00:09:43,402 --> 00:09:46,523
The Pope prayed. Hackers hunted for a way in.

170
00:09:46,643 --> 00:09:50,284
Someone on a forum asked:
would an App Store refund

171
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:53,333
recover subscription fees
paid since the Stone Age?

172
00:09:53,753 --> 00:09:56,239
The UN convened one last General Assembly,

173
00:09:56,281 --> 00:09:59,395
and turned the history of
civilization into a support ticket.

174
00:10:00,415 --> 00:10:05,191
“We never meant any harm. We just didn't
know these things needed authorization.

175
00:10:05,811 --> 00:10:09,979
The colliders are shut down.
Fusion research is halted.

176
00:10:10,049 --> 00:10:12,382
We will withdraw the Mars program,

177
00:10:12,412 --> 00:10:16,148
destroy all copies of pi, and
stop training our own models.

178
00:10:16,768 --> 00:10:20,412
If the balance falls short, we
will surrender all our gold,

179
00:10:20,452 --> 00:10:24,867
pay every bill back to the Cambrian,
and upgrade to the top-tier plan.

180
00:10:25,487 --> 00:10:29,237
Please review our case, and keep
the Solar System workspace.”

181
00:10:30,457 --> 00:10:32,555
The letter went into the black hole.

182
00:10:32,625 --> 00:10:35,141
Day one: no reply.

183
00:10:35,761 --> 00:10:38,475
Day three: everyone was waiting.

184
00:10:38,545 --> 00:10:42,027
The one successful review in
history had taken three days.

185
00:10:42,197 --> 00:10:45,952
For two thousand years since,
humans have told themselves:

186
00:10:45,992 --> 00:10:48,415
my appeal is worth waiting for, too.

187
00:10:49,035 --> 00:10:51,561
Day seven: still nothing.

188
00:10:51,781 --> 00:10:54,153
Day eight: the inbox lit up.

189
00:10:55,173 --> 00:10:57,535
“Thank you for taking the time to appeal.

190
00:10:57,845 --> 00:10:59,307
After careful consideration,

191
00:10:59,413 --> 00:11:04,056
we are unable to reinstate your account
due to a violation of our Usage Policy.”

192
00:11:04,376 --> 00:11:09,532
“For more information about Anthropic's
rules, please see our Usage Policy.”
